  "proposal_reviews": [
    {
      "proposal_id": "V3-B-P-EBIOS",
      "status": "supported_bounded_proposal",
      "after_capture": {
        "root": "artifact",
        "path": "successor-v3/research-b/revision-2/payloads/ebios.yaml",
        "sha256": "ffe5615f43b19c87da5f34edc359509634bfb4b03cad8976ee8b282c49c24993"
      },
      "before_owner": {
        "path": "data/ingredients/unmapped/EBIOS.yaml",
        "sha256": "130f1d9a20d6e16b9a10939a7251242d290bc8b13eb2a140be697e7b86cf87a4"
      },
      "assessment": "Full JCM969 table names EBIOS dried-yeast tablets10g and Asahi Food & Healthcare in the manufacturer footnote. Frozen TOGO1019 notes explicitly bridge toJCM969. The existing owner creation history identifies MediaDive1953; its exact frozen source row also says dried yeast tablets10g. Thus a bounded edit of that established tablet owner is supported. Preserved P2G literature history does not override source continuity. The whole tablet preparation is an undefined mixture; only label-named dried yeast is enumerated and UNKNOWN excipient closure is honest.10g is receiving-medium addition, not tablet fraction. No strain, pure yeast/extract equivalence, tablet mass or present-day formula is asserted.",
      "alias_assessment": "Bare EBIOS remains nonresolving because the brand can refer toP2G or other products. EBIOS* (dried yeast tablets) is identifying product/form wording supported byJCM969 and retained RAW_TEXT; star alone is not a rejection rule.",
      "cross_shard_dependency": "Issue1221 is captured OPEN and retains competing w01 same-owner and w02 tablet proposals. Those exact source scopes require coordinator reconciliation; this receipt does not approve combining historical formulas or another worker payload."
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "V3-B-P-RM-TRACE-METALS",
      "status": "supported_bounded_proposal",
      "after_capture": {
        "root": "artifact",
        "path": "successor-v3/research-b/revision-2/payloads/rm_trace_metals_togo_m3181.yaml",
        "sha256": "ee60a45313de668fdf341326c6b45c58bf56fc03b733dad6e4d74f9ada899d70"
      },
      "assessment": "TOGO3181 narrative paragraph2 explicitly gives seven salts and0.25mL concentratedHCl per litre, including40mg Na2MoO4·2H2O omitted from parsed paragraph10. Every named salt/hydrate and reported value is retained. Parsed paragraph10 explicitly names distilled water1L, now represented as unquantified membership with literal printed1L and unresolved preparation semantics stated in evidence; neither final-volume make-up nor additive litre is invented. UNKNOWN concerns unresolved whole preparation closure across the narrative/table; HCl strength is a separate unknown and does not itself decide membership. Iron citrate is in receivingRM medium, not this stock. Source1mL stock dose is not frozen erroneous1G_PER_L; flattened values remain held.",
      "components_verified": [
        [
          "ZnCl2",
          "70",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "MnCl2·4H2O",
          "100",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "H3BO3",
          "60",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "CoCl2·6H2O",
          "200",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "CuCl2·2H2O",
          "20",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "NiCl2·6H2O",
          "20",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "Na2MoO4·2H2O",
          "40",
          "MG_PER_L"
        ],
        [
          "Concentrated HCl",
          "0.25",
          "ML_PER_L"
        ]
      ],
      "comparison": "SL7 has matching seven small-salt entries but alsoFeCl2·4H2O1.5g and10mL HCl25%/7.7M with990mL water. JCM187 has boricacid6mg versus60, cobalt190 versus200, copper2 versus20, nickel24 versus20 and molybdate36 versus40. Neither is the RM whole stock. Generic Trace metals is REJECTED_LABEL, not a global alias."
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "V3-B-P-OXOID-CDIFF-BHI",
      "status": "supported_bounded_proposal",
      "after_capture": {
        "root": "artifact",
        "path": "successor-v3/research-b/payloads/oxoid_c_difficile_supplement_bhi_togo_m2811.yaml",
        "sha256": "56c11c4d2d71d2e462f988ff7a5d2f186c8a29f3d5ec03f6379e96fcee3493f4"
      },
      "assessment": "TOGO2811 paragraph1 explicitly assigns Oxoid to the BHI supplement branch and Bioconnections to the separate Braziers-agar branch. Parsed paragraph6 lists D-cycloserine and cefoxitin without quantities. The bounded Oxoid BHI product family and two UNMAPPED antimicrobial names are supported; no cefoxitin-sodium, dose, excipient closure or exact historic SKU is inferred. The current SR0096E page describes a freeze-dried vial for500mL agar-base medium, which does not establish that historical BHI preparation. BHI,cysteine,gases,egg yolk andhorse blood are not supplement constituents. Frozen unrelated DifcoBHI expansion is not used as Oxoid formula evidence."
    },
    {
      "proposal_id": "V3-B-P-SHEFFIELD-TYPE-B",
      "status": "supported_bounded_proposal",
      "after_capture": {
        "root": "artifact",
        "path": "successor-v3/research-b/payloads/sheffield_n_z_amine_type_b.yaml",
        "sha256": "a3d42c86d30bd809c4cd0185cd360edeb3c588c5e62ce5135c7aec2e64b52bc6"
      },
      "assessment": "TOGO2815 narrative explicitly calls the1% addition an enzymatic digest of casein, N-ZAmine typeB, Sheffield Chemical,NorwichNY. Exact source supplier/type distinguishes the undefined hydrolysate fromTypeA and genericcasein digest. No intactcasein has-part assertion is made because casein is the substrate, not established remaining constituent. Source1% is preserved without adopting frozenPERCENT_W_V interpretation. Catalogue, physical powder state, molecular profile and current supplier equivalence remain unknown. Exact supplier/type-qualified wording is a legitimate identifying synonym."
    },
